# No external CDN for runtime assets

## Rule (must)

Do **not** load fonts, stylesheets, or scripts from a CDN or any third-party URL at **runtime** in the app UI.

All of the following must come from **this repository** (or build output copied from it):

- Web fonts (`@font-face`, `fonts.googleapis.com`, `gstatic.com`, etc.)
- CSS (`<link rel="stylesheet" href="https://...">`, `@import url("https://...")`)
- JavaScript (`<script src="https://...">`)

## Allowed

- Relative / same-origin paths: `assets/`, `web/`, `build/web/`, `icons/`, `flutter_bootstrap.js`, `canvaskit/` (local Flutter web renderer), etc.
- Flutter: `pubspec.yaml` `fonts:` and `assets:`; Material/Cupertino icons bundled by Flutter
- Flutter web builds **must** use `--no-web-resources-cdn` so CanvasKit is bundled under `build/web/canvaskit/` with `useLocalCanvasKit: true`. Post-build `_flutter-web-no-cdn.ps1` strips any remaining CDN literals from deploy output and fails the build if any CDN host remains (zero CDN policy).
- WPF: local `Themes/`, embedded resources, system fonts
- Dependencies installed at **build time** (pub, NuGet) — not fetched from CDN when the user opens the app
- `url_launcher` / hyperlinks that open external sites in the browser (not embedding CDN assets in the app shell)

## Forbidden examples

```html
<!-- BAD -->
<link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=..." rel="stylesheet">
<script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/..."></script>
```

```css
/* BAD */
@import url("https://cdn.example.com/theme.css");
```

## Good examples

```html
<!-- GOOD -->
<link rel="stylesheet" href="styles/app.css">
<script src="flutter_bootstrap.js"></script>
```

```yaml
# GOOD — Flutter pubspec.yaml
flutter:
  fonts:
    - family: MyFont
      fonts:
        - asset: assets/fonts/MyFont-Regular.ttf
```

```powershell
# GOOD — Flutter web (local CanvasKit, no gstatic CDN)
flutter build web --release --no-web-resources-cdn
flutter run -d web-server --web-port=5320 --web-hostname=127.0.0.1 --no-web-resources-cdn
```

## Completion check

Before merging UI changes, search touched HTML/CSS/JS/XAML-WebView templates for `http://`, `https://`, `cdn`, `googleapis`, `gstatic`, `unpkg`, `jsdelivr`. Replace with local assets and document new files under `assets/` or `web/`.
